this directory is the host side of the tree: the simulators, the
libraries and tools that run on the host, and the source tree they build
for.  the top level make drives it:

	make		# bin/sim, bin/d1, then src/make
	make test	# the recovered 1.4 shell, on the user mode simulator

src/GNUmakefile recurses into lib, tools and usersim.  hwsim is not in
that list: the decision 1 machine is built by the top level d1 target,
which knows the monitor roms it has to assemble first.

directories:

micronix:
	the native source tree, the same tree /usr/src holds on the
	machine.  headers, libc and libunix, the ccc compiler passes,
	the commands and the kernel.  it builds two ways and has two
	makefiles: GNUmakefile on the host with the cross toolchain
	(mxccc, mxar), makefile inside micronix with the installed one.
		sys/		the kernel and its notes: ARCHITECTURE.md,
				DISKLABEL.md, FEATURES-2.md, INTR.md,
				MEDIACHG.md, NET.md
		stand/		the bootstrap loaders and the monitor roms
		libexec/	the passes ccc runs: pass0, c0, c1, peep, astpp
		cmd/		the commands, including ccc, cpp, ld and asz
		lib/		libc, libunix, libutil, libccc, fslib
		include/	the system headers
		dev/		devlist, the device nodes mkfs and create_vol
		etc/		the seed files for /etc
		cpm/		CP/M's header tree, /usr/cpm/include
		man/		manual pages

hwsim:
	the behavioral S-100 machine.  hwsim.c, s100.c and mediachg.c
	are the machine independent core; hwsim/d1 holds the MPZ80
	board, the console and clock, the monitor interface, and one .c
	per card.  the card list is DRIVERS in hwsim/d1/GNUmakefile.
	d1 is the debug build; d1p is the NODEBUG=1 performance build,
	which d1 execs with -P.  ARCHITECTURE.md is the sketch for
	making the boards pluggable.

usersim:
	the user mode simulator.  it hosts micronix system calls on the
	host and runs against the filesystem/ directory, with no
	simulated hardware and no disk images.  it is built here and
	run from the top of the tree, where its default root lives:
	src/usersim/sim, or bin/sim.

lib:
	the host libraries, folded into libsim.a: the disassembler, the
	syscall formatter, the monitor and debugger, gui, imd, json,
	lockfile, and fslib.  fslibfunc.c is compiled out of
	micronix/lib so that the host tools and the guest agree on the
	filesystem; unused/ is the road not taken.

tools:
	host tools.  filesystem: dcheck, icheck, ncheck, fsck, readall.
	images: imd, imdd, dumpsec.  objects: nm, size, ar, disas, dump,
	doc, zmac.  provisioning: mnix (format, label, mkfs) and hwsim
	(which drives the simulator from sim.json).  the latter two are
	described in PROVISION.md.

include:
	headers shared by the host code.

attic:
	retired sources, kept for reference.  z80emu is the instruction
	simulator the machine used before the current core.

objects, binaries and the occasional logfile are built in place beside
their sources; they are gitignored, not checked in.  the top level
README is the account of what this tree is and how it differs from the
1.61 kernel it came from.
